{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`.\n\n**Same result fields as the originating tool**\n- `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` compares every search match entry exactly (node, file, selector, excerpt, tag). It also checks `complete` and a UUID `search_id` on every page.\n- `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` checks `node` on every outline page. It checks `file`, `selector` and `kind` on every item.\n- `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` checks `node` and `data` for each listed file across pages.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` checks `node.selector` on continuation pages.\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` and the root read in the outline test check the `file`, `selector` and `text` fields on read pages.\n\n**Text reads return successive portions**\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` concatenates the pages. The result must equal the original text, which contains multi-byte `é` characters, even though the contents change after preparation.\n- The root read in the outline test and `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` do the same for source reads.\n\n**Listings, outlines and searches return whole entries in original order**\n- The search test requires every one of the 350 original matches, in order and with none missing or duplicated, even though the file is overwritten after the first delivery.\n- The outline test requires 401 items in order with the correct selectors. The children on the read pages must match the outline items.\n- The listing test requires all 2000 files in order, even though a file is added after the first page.\n\n**Only a page with a successor includes `next`**\n- Every pagination loop ends exactly when `next` is absent, and the tests assert that more than one page was produced.\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` asserts `next` is present exactly on page 0 of 2.\n- The search test checks `count == lines.len()` at the end, which would fail if a page lacked `next` while more entries remained.\n\n**Reusing a UUID returns the same page and the same successor**\n- `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` dispatches `get_next_page` with the same `next` a second time, after the file was rewritten and after the page was first delivered. It asserts the text is identical, which includes the successor UUID.\n- Reuse is exercised through the search tool only. The `get_next_page` path is shared by all tool kinds: `SessionTools::dispatch` sends every call to `self.pages.get`. I treat this as sufficient.\n\n**Errors for malformed, unknown and foreign UUIDs**\n- In the outline test, `get_next_page` with `\"invalid\"` (malformed) and `\"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\"` (unknown) both return errors.\n- In the search test, a peer session's `get_next_page` with a UUID from another session returns an error.\n- `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` covers a foreign UUID in a populated peer conversation for graph tools. It is marked with `tool_agent.isolation`, which `pages.behavior` cites.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "1ac80069e6c37d2808f2a07935fa541926528e3931df8b3a2c423e0fed2a9800",
